{
  "_about": "London's lighting (the owner, 2026-11-15: screenshots 20-43-49, 20-43-58, 20-44-40 and 20-45-05). Its ten window reflection probes (reflection_window, reflection_window(1) to (9)) go: they have affect_diffuse false, which no stock 0.26g probe has, and 0.26g's shader for it writes the surface's own colour into the ambient light, so white walls glowed in their slabs, a halo ran round the wall hole and bright strips beside the boarded windows. The corridor probe gerkin(4) takes its neighbour gerkin(3)'s cubemap: its own has the fluorescent lamp's lavender light baked in, which stayed once the lamp was shot out. In all five projects (docs/notes/map-probes.md).",
